```
Hunt of the week #1 (DRAFT FOR REVIEW, untested): PHP worker or web server spawning a shell or download tool
Splunk equivalent of query.kql, using the CIM Endpoint data model (Processes dataset) populated by
an EDR, Sysmon for Linux or auditd add-on. Starting point only: tune for your estate before use.
Hunt ID: 2026-10-22-php-web-server-spawning-shell | ATT&CK: T1190, T1059.004, T1105, T1505.003
Source:  https://github.com/CyberThreatNet/hunt-lab | Licence: MIT - see LICENSE
tstats cannot use regex, so it pre-filters on "php*" and the where clause applies the exact pattern.
```
| tstats summariesonly=false allow_old_summaries=true
    count min(_time) as FirstSeen max(_time) as LastSeen
    values(Processes.user) as Accounts values(Processes.process) as SampleCommands
    from datamodel=Endpoint.Processes
    where (Processes.parent_process_name="php*"
        OR Processes.parent_process_name IN ("httpd", "apache2", "frankenphp", "lsphp"))
      AND Processes.process_name IN ("sh", "bash", "dash", "curl", "wget", "nc", "ncat", "perl", "python3", "base64")
    by Processes.dest Processes.parent_process_name Processes.parent_process Processes.process_name
| rename "Processes.*" as "*"
| where match(parent_process_name, "^php(-fpm|-cgi)?[0-9.]*$")
    OR parent_process_name IN ("httpd", "apache2", "frankenphp", "lsphp")
``` Tuning: add exclusions for known-good activity here, e.g. | search NOT SampleCommands="*/usr/sbin/sendmail*" ```
| convert ctime(FirstSeen) ctime(LastSeen)
| sort 0 FirstSeen
| table FirstSeen LastSeen dest parent_process_name parent_process process_name Accounts SampleCommands count
